sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila novamexicana 1.9 µm Turing wavelength (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 72.7/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg kinetics at a=0.10, b=0.90, Dv/Du=24, gamma=1 select λ_c=1.901 µm. Trace=-0.20, det=1, σ_max=0.306, equal-diffusion σ_max=-0.103. The homogeneous spot lattice in the comparison figure does not resemble the vendored spiral. Predecessor mojavensis γ=1.79 → 1.421 µm; successor orena γ=2.60 → 1.179 µm. Dispersion Pearson r=1.0 against numpy eigenvalues. Overall 72.7/100 (faithfulness 67.3, reproducibility 85.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 46, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_novamexicana_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 683187 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 98e808f4353c030a22bda33219173888a7746fa739b0ab10e980a085fb397c97 (sha256 98e808f4353c030a22bda33219173888a7746fa739b0ab10e980a085fb397c97), spec_fingerprint a0f21a8e3413d8812c132cbd2d8ce478b6a0e92dd2f6706500aa4eab75fc7b6a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a0f21a8e3413d8812c132cbd2d8ce478b6a0e92dd2f6706500aa4eab75fc7b6a; artifact_sha256: 98e808f4353c030a22bda33219173888a7746fa739b0ab10e980a085fb397c97; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_novamexicana_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_novamexicana_specimen.jpg=43cdce899b1abe8b...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the requirement that inhibitor diffusion exceed activator diffusion. | Schnakenberg 1979 trimolecular kinetics f=a-u+u^2 v, g=b-u^2 v. | Murray 1981 reaction-rate scale: chemical wavelength shortens as gamma^{-1/2}. | Wittkopp et al. 2009: the pale abdominal cuticle of D. novamexicana relative to D. americana is caused in large part by cis-regulatory alleles of ebony and tan. | Lamb et al. 2020: ebony contributes to pigmentation divergence between D. americana and D. novamexicana.; reconstructed_in_script: gamma triple (1.00, 1.79, 2.60) at the assigned 1.901 µm scale. Not a published measurement and not the sibling slots' alpha_scale values. | Diffusion ratio 24 chosen so the cleared discriminant 91^2-2400 is positive.; transfer_boundary: Allan & Matzkin 2019 and Comeault et al. 2017 identify the predecessor and successor species. They do not measure a 1.9 µm pigment spacing.; does_not_claim: That 1.901 µm was measured on a novamexicana micrograph. | That the species-gallery asset is a SEM of pigment granules. Wikimedia Commons had no CC photograph. | That mojavensis and orena are anagenetic ancestors. They are chronoseries neighbors 24/41 at 0 Ma.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [model_equation/model-fidelity, pressure P=1.9]: Homogeneous a does not carry the vendored optical-density field.",
            "open need [morphometric_validation/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=1.1]: Tabulate simulated predecessor wavelength against 12/sqrt(1.79).",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=1.9]: Score the published last frame against the vendored image, not only the homogeneous spot lattice.",
            "remediation needed: Drive basal production a(x) with the vendored cuticle field so the PDE steady state, not only a post-hoc multiply, carries the specimen's large-scale structure.",
            "remediation needed: Publish the specimen-calibrated GIF as the scored animation and recompute CV similarity, Pearson r, RMSE and KS on that frame.",
            "remediation needed: Report the predecessor simulation's dominant wavelength in pixels against the Murray prediction 12/sqrt(1.79)." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.727"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-assessor pass 1)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000> .
}

